                                    "text": "6",
                                    "textcolor": [ 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 ]
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "bubble": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-87",
                                    "linecount": 10,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 965.0, 40.0, 360.0, 145.0 ],
                                    "text": "The closer the frequencies are to nyquist, and the greater gain they are, the more foldback aliasing will occur. If you cannot hear it, it does not mean that it is not bad. Aliasing stays in your audio chain and there is nothing you can do to get rid of it, not even filtering, and it will greatly affect your final output, masking the audio you actually want. In this tab we chose some unrealistic extreme cases to demonstrate the effect. But your audio will likely have many more harmonics in it than a cosine wave! In the next tabs we compare aliasing with antialiased saturation..."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "bubble": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-85",
                                    "linecount": 8,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 89.0, 560.0, 246.0, 118.0 ],
                                    "text": "Select the 6th preset. Our spectral display is linear, focussing on high frequencies. Our frequency and gain are high. There should be just one additional harmonic here, but as you can see there are hundreds of artifacts filling the audio spectrum, both above and below our fundamental frequency."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "bubble": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-84",
                                    "linecount": 7,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 89.0, 451.0, 339.0, 104.0 ],
                                    "text": "Select the 5th preset. Our cycle~ frequency increased to over 6kHz, our gain at +20dB. We can see the waveshape and the aliasing and it is difficult to tell which are harmonics and which are aliased foldover. And we can hear it. It sounds horrible and grainy. Move the gain number box up and down to see and hear the effect. Do not listen for too long, it is bad for your ears."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "bgcolor": [ 1.0, 0.392156862745098, 0.0, 1.0 ],
                                    "fontname": "Arial Bold",
