                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 10.0, 70.0, 660.0, 84.0 ],
                                    "text": "Saturation is good. Aliasing is bad. Saturation adds harmonics to your audio. Adding harmonics to your audio causes aliasing. Aliasing is a mathematical fact. It is not an opinion and not an aesthetic. It is just bad. It destroys your audio and will destroy your music especially if performing through a full range PA. It needs to be managed, just as you would manage bass and headroom. In this tab we just go through the basics for the sake of completeness. In further tabs we look at antialiasing in evieve.",
